From: TortOS-px2
Subject: [PATCH] bootstage marks for timing U-Boot without serial

Marks after the init steps most likely to be slow, so the record U-Boot
leaves in the device tree (CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_FDT) shows where its startup
time goes. The tree is shrunk to its minimum before that record is
written, which left room for only four entries, so the shrink now keeps
4 KiB spare. Development only.
---
--- a/boot/image-fdt.c	2025-10-06 19:13:09.000000000 +0000
+++ b/boot/image-fdt.c	2026-10-01 05:10:15.353680015 +0000
@@ -693,7 +693,8 @@
 	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(LMB) && lmb)
 		lmb_free(map_to_sysmem(blob), fdt_totalsize(blob), LMB_NONE);
 
-	ret = fdt_shrink_to_minimum(blob, 0);
+	/* TortOS-px2: leave room for the bootstage record added after this */
+	ret = fdt_shrink_to_minimum(blob, 4096);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err;
 	of_size = ret;
